{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1465468270,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNTkzNzYwMzE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/517","origin":"github"},"title":"Remove from annex","message":"I just unified the behaviour of `remove` in `AnnexRepo` and `GitRepo` class. Currently this is just a `git rm` in both cases (just an override to respect direct mode in case of `AnnexRepo`). I wonder whether this is what we want. For the \"opposing\" operation `add`, we execute an `annex add`or a `git add` respectively. Shouldn't we therefore have a `remove`, that in the same way distinguishes between `git annex unannex` and `git rm` as the complementary operation to `add`? What do you think, @yarikoptic @hanke ?","files":null}]}